tle traction in any survey"], "rationale": "Polls average roughly 23-24 points for Shapiro, with even Republican-sponsored Susquehanna showing a 21-point race, and all eight raters call the race Solid or Safe D. Markets price Shapiro at 98-99%, so a large but slightly tempered margin near 20 points fits the evidence.", "watch": "A late polling miss or unusually strong Republican turnout could narrow the margin, though the outcome itself is unlikely to flip.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor race pits incumbent Democrat Josh Shapiro against Republican state official Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Polling throughout the fall has been remarkably consistent, showing Shapiro ahead by roughly 20 to 30 points across pollsters of varied sponsorship, including a Republican-leaning firm. Averages put the race near 23 points, and prediction markets price Shapiro's chances at about 98 to 99 percent.\n\nEvery major race rater, from the Cook Political Report to Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column. Shapiro's incumbency, fundraising edge, and the state's recent Democratic strength in statewide races all point the same direction. The main open question is the size of the win, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0}, {"dat